 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Color Space:** Colors must be converted from sRGB to linear RGB before encoding into $f\_dc$ because the renderer applies a linear-to-sRGB display transform [S1, unofficial]. Failure to do so results in incorrect colors [S1, unofficial].
+- **Color Space:** Colors must be converted from sRGB to linear RGB before encoding into $f\_dc$ because the renderer applies a linear-to-sRGB display transform [S1, unofficial].
 - **Activation Inversion:** The parser expects inverted activations. Scales are stored as $\ln(\sigma)$, $f\_dc$ as $(c_{lin}-0.5)/SH\_C0$, opacity as $\logit(p)$, and rotation as scalar-first $w,x,y,z$ [S1, unofficial].
-- **Division by Zero:** The Fibonacci sphere formula uses $n-1$ in the denominator. If $n=1$, this causes a division by zero. The method assumes $n > 1$ [S1, unofficial].
+- **Division by Zero:** The Fibonacci sphere formula uses $n-1$ in the denominator. If $n=1$, this causes a division by zero. The method assumes $n > 1$ [S1, G, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(n)$, where $n$ is the number of Gaussians. Each Gaussian requires constant-time mathematical operations [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(n)$ for the output PLY file size ($14 \times 4 \times n$ bytes plus header) [S1, unofficial].
